+ * The STOPPED half is asserted. sgen calls sgen_client_collection_end before sgen_restart_world
+ * clears world_is_stopped, so sgen_is_world_stopped () is TRUE there and the definition in
+ * sgen-mono.c checks it -- which doubles as the tripwire against moving the call back into
+ * sgen_client_restart_world, where the flag has already been cleared and where non-collection
+ * stop-the-worlds arrive too.
+ *
+ * The FINISHED half cannot be asserted at all: sgen clears sgen_current_collection_generation at
+ * the end of the minor/major collection function, so it reads -1 here exactly as it does outside
+ * a collection. Do not reintroduce that assertion. The CALL SITE is what establishes it, and
+ * sgen_client_collection_end exists so that the site cannot be a stop-the-world which never
+ * collected.
